## 7. YOLOV8 PPE DETECTION ENGINE

Use Ultralytics YOLOv8 in the Python backend.

Implement a modular detection service with functions for:
- Loading the configured model
- Validating model availability
- Detecting persons
- Detecting supported PPE classes
- Returning bounding boxes and confidence scores
- Associating PPE with workers
- Processing image uploads
- Processing video frames
- Saving annotated output
- Aggregating video observations
- Creating structured detection results

Support configurable classes such as:
- person
- helmet / hardhat
- safety vest / reflective vest
- gloves
- safety shoes / boots
- goggles
- mask
- missing helmet, if explicitly supported by the model
- missing vest, if explicitly supported by the model
- other classes supported by the configured dataset

IMPORTANT MODEL REQUIREMENTS:

A standard COCO-pretrained YOLOv8 model is not a PPE-compliance model. Do not claim that it can reliably detect missing helmets, reflective vests, or gloves.

Provide a configuration variable such as PPE_MODEL_PATH pointing to the actual trained weights.

Allow a model file such as models/best.pt to be configured.

Document the expected model class names and model training requirements.

If no PPE-trained model is installed:
- Show a clear warning in the UI.
- Allow a demo mode for general object detection if useful.
- Do not produce fabricated PPE compliance scores.
- Do not treat an undetected helmet as proof that a worker has no helmet.
- Display PPE results as “Unavailable” or “Unable to verify” when appropriate.
- Never generate fake violation records just to populate the dashboard.

Use a pluggable detection adapter so that a compatible trained PPE model can be replaced without rewriting the whole application.

For video analysis, save the frame timestamp for each relevant detection and use a stable track identifier when tracking is available. Explain that a track ID is a temporary visual tracking identifier, not a verified real-world identity.

